  "claim": "James Nestor is a writer of historical fiction. He has written for a publication that was published after the publication responsible for the Global Open Access Forum.",
  "evidencia": "Page: American Scientist. Sentence: American Scientist (informally abbreviated AmSci) is an American bimonthly science and technology magazine published since 1913 by Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society.\nPage: Dwell (magazine). Sentence: It was launched with a magazine in September 2000 to bridge the gap between design professionals and enthusiasts by Lara Hedberg Deam with architecture and design critic Karrie Jacobs as its Editor-in-Chief.\nPage: Global Open Access Forum. Sentence: It was created by the American Scientist, which is published by Sigma Xi, in September 1998, before the term \"Open Access\" (OA) was coined, and it was originally called the \"September98-Forum.\"\nPage: James Nestor (writer). Sentence: James Nestor is a San Francisco-based journalist who has written for \"Outside magazine\", \"Men's Journal\", \"Dwell\" magazine, National Public Radio, \"The New York Times\", the San Francisco Chronicle magazine, and others.",
