        "original_id": "4e2ef5b9-c9d7-5e89-b676-5a08da9e3f3f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: American Scientist, Dwell, Global Open Access Forum\n- Organizations: Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society, National Public Radio, The New York Times\n- People: Lara Hedberg Deam, Karrie Jacobs, James Nestor\n- Places: San Francisco\n- Topics: science and technology magazines, open access, journalism\n\nFacts:\n- American Scientist is an American bimonthly science and technology magazine that has been published since 1913 by Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society.\n- The Global Open Access Forum was created by American Scientist in September 1998, before the term Open Access was coined, and it was originally called the September98-Forum.\n- Dwell was launched as a magazine in September 2000 by Lara Hedberg Deam to bridge the gap between design professionals and enthusiasts, with Karrie Jacobs as Editor-in-Chief.\n- James Nestor is a San Francisco-based journalist who has written for Dwell, National Public Radio, The New York Times, Outside magazine, Men's Journal, and the San Francisco Chronicle magazine.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
